// @ens-test
// @exit 2
// @stdout-contains PASS first test passes
// @stderr-contains panic: boom
// @stderr-contains crash_test.ens
// @stderr-contains stopped before it had run every test
// @stderr-contains the next test after them
// A panic in the second test ends the whole run. The first result is already on
// standard output, because the run's streams belong to the command and a result
// appears as the test producing it finishes; the panic reaches standard error
// straight from the runner, and the command adds what the code it ended with
// means and how to find the test that ended it.
